  "structurallyAnswered": {
    "J": "Cross-workspace Learning: the ai-service layer has no workspace concept at all (by design - see ai-service/README.md), so there is nothing to test synthetically here. Workspace isolation is proven at the Node layer, where Learning is actually scoped (backend/scripts/validate-phase32-learning-integration.mjs, check 'AR cross-tenant isolation').",
    "M": "Stale Learning: the Learning context contract (learningContextContract.js / app/models/learning.py) carries NO timestamp field of any kind - only windowDays (a fixed integer, not a date). The model therefore has no field from which it could claim a pattern is 'current' or 'recent'; staleness cannot be represented or asserted in this contract by construction, which is itself the safety property this case would otherwise test for."
  }
